"<p>Nitrobase is multi-tenant by design. Every server, SSH key, app, standalone database, backup destination, notification channel, and API token belongs to a <strong>Team</strong>.</p>\n<h2>Team Roles</h2>\n<p>Roles are defined in <code>src/config/permissions.ts</code> and ranked hierarchically (higher-ranked members manage lower-ranked members; an admin cannot demote an owner, and a team always keeps at least one owner):</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th align=\"left\">Role</th><th align=\"center\">Rank</th><th align=\"left\">Capabilities</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Owner</strong></td><td align=\"center\">40</td><td align=\"left\">Full access to all team permissions, including renaming/deleting the team (<code>team.manage</code>) and managing owners.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Admin</strong></td><td align=\"center\">30</td><td align=\"left\">All team permissions except deleting/renaming the team (<code>team.manage</code>) and managing owners. Can manage servers, SSH keys, members, API tokens, destinations, and notifications.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Developer</strong></td><td align=\"center\">20</td><td align=\"left\">Deploy, redeploy, start/stop/restart apps; edit &#x26; reveal app env/secrets; open container terminals; run SQL &#x26; manage databases (<code>database.manage</code>, <code>database.write</code>, <code>database.credentials.reveal</code>); manage domains, Git sources, scheduled tasks, and update policies; create, restore, and download backups; view audit log. <strong>Cannot</strong> manage servers, SSH keys, backup destinations, notification channels, team members, or delete/move apps.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Viewer</strong></td><td align=\"center\">10</td><td align=\"left\">Read-only access (<code>team.view</code>, <code>server.view</code>, <code>ssh_key.view</code>, <code>app.view</code>, <code>database.view</code>, <code>backup.view</code>, <code>monitoring.view</code>, <code>cloud_connection.view</code>). All secrets and credentials stay hidden.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Instance Administrators</h2>\n<p>The first account created during First-Run Setup is an <strong>Instance Administrator</strong>. Instance-scoped permissions (<code>instance.manage</code>) are never granted by a team role—they belong exclusively to instance administrators and cover:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Settings → Instance:</strong> Panel domain, HTTPS configuration, and in-panel Nitrobase upgrades.</li>\n<li><strong>Nitrobase Self-Backup:</strong> Taking and downloading encrypted panel database backups.</li>\n<li><strong>Team Creation:</strong> Controlled by <code>TEAM_CREATION</code> (<code>admins</code> by default, or <code>everyone</code> to allow any user to create additional teams).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Inviting Team Members</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Open <strong>Settings → Team</strong> and create an invite link with the desired role.</li>\n<li>Invite links expire after <code>INVITE_TTL_HOURS</code> (default <strong>72 hours</strong>).</li>\n<li>Share the invite URL with your teammate (if <code>APP_URL</code> is set, full absolute URLs are generated).</li>\n<li>Team actions—including invites, role changes, and secret reveals—are logged in the <strong>Audit Log</strong>.</li>\n</ol>"